%% Payment State Diagram — PayLink
%% Rules that make this diagram correct:
%%  - Unknown is NOT refunded automatically: the biller may already have the money.
%%  - Unknown resolves only through reconciliation, to Completed or to Refunded.
%%  - Completed, Rejected and Refunded are final.
%%  - A Failed payment always releases its hold, so it passes through Refunded.
%%  - Retrying with the same idempotencyKey is not a state change.

stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Initiated : customer submits payment

    Initiated --> Rejected : fraud check blocks
    Initiated --> Rejected : insufficient funds
    Initiated --> Rejected : invalid bill reference

    Initiated --> FundsHeld : wallet hold succeeds
    FundsHeld --> SentToBiller : request accepted by biller

    SentToBiller --> Completed : biller confirms
    SentToBiller --> Failed : biller declines
    SentToBiller --> Unknown : timeout or ambiguous reply

    Failed --> Refunded : hold released
    Unknown --> Completed : reconciliation confirms payment
    Unknown --> Refunded : reconciliation confirms failure

    Completed --> [*]
    Rejected --> [*]
    Refunded --> [*]

    note right of Unknown
        Money stays held.
        Never auto-refunded.
        Resolved by reconciliation only.
    end note

    note right of Completed
        Hold captured into a ledger debit.
        Final state.
    end note
